<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  Receive buffers big enough for this robot's camera.

  Measured on 2026-09-07, mid-run, on the NUC:

      net.core.rmem_max = 212992           (the Linux default, 208 KB)
      colour image       = 640x360 BGR8    (691 KB per frame, at 30 simulated Hz)
      UDP RcvbufErrors   = 3,119,527 and rising by about 200 a second

  One image is more than three times the whole socket receive buffer, so it is
  fragmented into hundreds of datagrams, and a buffer that small overflows
  continuously. Losing any one fragment discards the entire frame.

  What that looked like from the outside: perception ran happily for 68 simulated
  seconds and then reported "no camera images arrived at all in the last 10 s" for the
  rest of the run, while `ros2 topic hz` on the same topic from a freshly created
  subscriber reported a healthy 30 frames a simulated second. The camera was fine. The
  reader had stopped being able to reassemble anything. Every answer perception gave
  after that was about a stored frame, so the robot centred on a book that was no longer
  where it thought, and the approach flapped between centring and searching until it
  timed out.

  The socket size CycloneDDS asks for is capped by net.core.rmem_max, so this file is
  only half the fix. tools/sim raises that limit when it starts the container, which
  it can do because the container is privileged and on the host network.

  Defrag limits are raised to match: with hundreds of fragments per sample and several
  samples in flight, the default of four unreliable samples under reassembly is not
  enough to survive a burst.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config"
            xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
            xsi:schemaLocation="https://cdds.io/config
                                https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eclipse-cyclonedds/cyclonedds/master/etc/cyclonedds.xsd">
  <Domain id="any">
    <Internal>
      <MinimumSocketReceiveBufferSize>32MB</MinimumSocketReceiveBufferSize>
      <DefragUnreliableMaxSamples>128</DefragUnreliableMaxSamples>
      <DefragReliableMaxSamples>128</DefragReliableMaxSamples>
    </Internal>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
